  "body": "@AKSHAYSHARMAJS is implementing the standard for Python (https://github.com/scrapy/xtractmime), and we find the webM parsing algorithm rather confusing.\r\n\r\nOur confusion did not stem from what was reported in https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/93, though, but from the return value of the algorithm to parse vint. The algorithm states that 2 values are returned, but only 1 of those values is actually used by the calling algorithm. So the vint-parsing algorithm could be cut in half, and it would not only be simpler, but way more clear.",
